Z||000000||Fearless Freep||11-11-2000||05:38 PM||||Have a 98 camaro with just the factory tape deck from delco electronics.  I wanted to add a FM modulator/cd changer to the stock radio.  Picked up a nice 6 disk changer for about 85.00.  Problem is, the antena connection in the back of the radio is "smaller" than the standard sized antena ports.  I know that I can get an adapter to change the size of the antena cable to the larger format (which will plug into the modulator) but I still have to have a cable that runs from the modulator to the head unit!  Basically, I need an adapter that will change the standard down to a smaller.  Anybody???????||||reg||1
Z||000001||DrRodey||11-11-2000||05:41 PM||||:Yeah that sounds about like how i had to do it in my Grand Prix when i had it..... Sucks but it needs to be done.<P>You can get all the necesarry parts at radio shack for like 10 bucks.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by DrRodey (edited 11-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||11-11-2000||06:15 PM||||Does anyone know if this can be used without hooking it up to the radio at all ?<P>If it's possible, I'd like to carry my changer around in a laptop case so I don't have to install it. And put it in the trunk when I'm not using it.<P>Will one of these "broadcast" if you plug an antenna into it ?||||reg||1
Z||000003||DrRodey||11-11-2000||09:13 PM||||No they have to be hooked up inline.  if you wanted you could run longer antenna cables and use inslated inline connectors for the power and ground and remove it when you wanted to but they will NOT  "broadcast" ||||reg||1
